// JupyterLab keyboard-shortcut overrides for presenting.
//
// Problem: Jupyter's default Shift+Enter is `notebook:run-cell-and-select-next`.
// The "select next" half is what moves you on -- when the next cell belongs to
// the next slide, RISE follows the selection and the deck jumps forward the
// instant the cell finishes. Mid-lecture that means you run a demo and never
// see its output.
//
// Fix: disable that binding and point Shift+Enter at `notebook:run-cell`, which
// runs the cell and leaves the selection (and therefore the slide) alone.
// Advance deliberately with Space / Right / Down instead.
//
// Ctrl+Enter and Cmd+Enter are already bound to `notebook:run-cell` by default,
// so they behave this way with or without this file.
//
// Installed by present.sh (into its isolated config dir) and by
// .devcontainer/setup.sh (into the container's ~/.jupyter). Delete either copy
// to get stock Shift+Enter behaviour back.
//
// Second problem, same cause: Left/Right arrows skipped whole slides.
//
// JupyterLab binds ArrowRight to `notebook:move-cursor-heading-below-or-expand`
// (and ArrowLeft to the -above- variant) in command mode. Those jump the active
// cell to the next/previous *markdown heading*, and RISE follows the active
// cell to whichever slide it lives on. Content slides start with a `##`
// heading, but the exercise cards and live-example banners are pure HTML with no
// heading -- so the arrows leapt straight over them. Measured on Lecture 4:
// one keypress went from slide 20 to 22, skipping the "Fruits Beginning with a
// Vowel" exercise entirely. `Space` was unaffected because it never reaches
// Lumino's keymap.
//
// Disabling both lets reveal.js handle the arrows natively, so they step one
// slide at a time like Space does.
{
  "shortcuts": [
    {
      "command": "notebook:move-cursor-heading-below-or-expand",
      "keys": ["ArrowRight"],
      "selector": ".jp-Notebook.jp-mod-commandMode:not(.jp-mod-readWrite) :focus",
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "command": "notebook:move-cursor-heading-above-or-collapse",
      "keys": ["ArrowLeft"],
      "selector": ".jp-Notebook.jp-mod-commandMode:not(.jp-mod-readWrite) :focus",
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "command": "notebook:run-cell-and-select-next",
      "keys": ["Shift Enter"],
      "selector": ".jp-Notebook.jp-mod-editMode",
      "disabled": true
    },
    {
      "command": "notebook:run-cell",
      "keys": ["Shift Enter"],
      "selector": ".jp-Notebook.jp-mod-editMode"
    },
    {
      "command": "notebook:run-cell",
      "keys": ["Shift Enter"],
      "selector": ".jp-Notebook.jp-mod-commandMode:not(.jp-mod-readWrite) :focus"
    }
  ]
}
